                     /note="P4 is a hexameric packaging NTPase which belongs to
                     the DnaB-like family. Though there is no sequence
                     similarity, the NTP binding domain bears striking
                     structural similarity to RecA/F1-ATPase-like motors. 12
                     hexamers of P4 are found at the 5-fold vertices of the
                     procapsid and use ATP hydrolysis to actively transport L, M
                     and S segments into the procapsid. RNA segments are
                     packaged in order."
